  "notes": "After winning the opening spade lead South should immediately ruff a spade. The only possible danger is a trump loser. If East has 4 clubs to the ♣J, an early spade ruff will be a necessary step in preparing for a trump coup.\n\nSouth should next draw 2 rounds of trumps, easily taking the balance if both defenders follow. When West shows out on the second round of clubs, South's early spade ruff will have been necessary.\n\nSouth must shorten his trumps 1 more time. If East began with 3334 distribution, South cannot go wrong. If East has only 2 spades, South must guess whether East has 2434 or 2344 distribution.\n\nSouth must cash 3 rounds of East's 3 card red suit ending in the dummy, before playing another spade and ruffing. Next South cashes 3 rounds of East's 4 card red suit ending in the dummy. East's ♣J is trump couped at trick 12.",
